{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":3885563,"ns":0,"title":"Bevel gear","extract":"Bevel gears are gears in which the axes of the two shafts intersect and the tooth-bearing faces of the gears themselves are conically shaped. Bevel gears are most often mounted on shafts that are 90 degrees apart, but can be designed to work at other angles as well.","description":"Cone- or frustum-shaped gears for shafts whose axes intersect","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}